# Architecture Overview — {{ project_name }}

This application is built on **Khaira Framework**'s opinionated 5-layer separation of concerns.

## The 5-Layer Pipeline

```text
HTTP Request
     │
     ▼
┌──────────────┐
│   Routers    │   FastAPI path operations, dependency injection, status codes
└──────┬───────┘
       │ delegates exclusively to
       ▼
┌──────────────┐
│   Services   │   Business domain logic, transactions, raises HTTP exceptions
└──────┬───────┘
       │ delegates data queries to
       ▼
┌──────────────┐
│ Repositories │   Database access queries, filtering, commits
└──────┬───────┘
       │ operates on
       ▼
┌──────────────┐
│    Models    │   SQLAlchemy ORM / Beanie ODM mapped classes
└──────────────┘
       ▲
       │ validated by
┌──────────────┐
│   Schemas    │   Pydantic v2 DTOs (Base, Create, Update, Response)
└──────────────┘
```

## Runtime Layer Enforcement
KairaApp validates that:
1. Routers never import repositories directly.
2. Cross-layer violations raise runtime `LayerViolationError` exceptions.
3. Services remain decoupled from transport protocols.
